From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:16:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] erhai config: build the SM8750 GPU clock controller in

With CONFIG_SM_GPUCC_8750=m the gpucc driver only appears once a module
loader runs, and an initramfs without one strands the whole GPU chain:
the GMU and GPU probe defer on clocks and power domains that never
arrive. Build it in so the GPU chain is available from early boot.

Link: https://github.com/yzddmr6/linux-sm8750-erhai/commit/bd4f02e3f76e97abb7c015fefaa71ef6cb1b340e
Signed-off-by: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/erhai_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/erhai_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/erhai_defconfig
index c29ac34627f..52f61d77f03 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/erhai_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/erhai_defconfig
@@ -827,7 +827,7 @@ CONFIG_SM_GPUCC_8350=m
 CONFIG_SM_GPUCC_8450=m
 CONFIG_SM_GPUCC_8550=m
 CONFIG_SM_GPUCC_8650=m
-CONFIG_SM_GPUCC_8750=m
+CONFIG_SM_GPUCC_8750=y
 CONFIG_SM_TCSRCC_8550=y
 CONFIG_SM_TCSRCC_8650=y
 CONFIG_SM_TCSRCC_8750=y
